{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128a3442836b030a555f413e56a493ac2b3039fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+5+\\cdots+2017+2019-2-4-6-\\cdots-2016-2018$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"486\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08dcb9844d7c5f39592c6e9dde3dd595bfb94b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }-1010\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }-1009\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }1008\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }1009\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }1010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"533\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rearranging the terms, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a523cf483f5125ad925d467cad6b8c65d41660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-2)+(3-4)+(5-6)+...(2017-2018)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"18\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2f7f38f5e9fc197760f34adb12d9cced4d18c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1009+2019=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"217\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>If you were stuck on this problem, refer to AoPS arithmetic lessons.\n</p><p>~Nivaar\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the last numbers of each of the sets (even numbers and odd numbers) have a difference of two. So, do the second last ones and so on. Now, all we need to find is the number of integers in any of the sets (I chose even) to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7ac3e0e7eb067564ed6c253320363efb3f78fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"82\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~avamarora\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is similar to the Solution 1: \nRearranging the terms, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e229e08780fa0068270b877d6c964c9c8fdc4075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+(3-2)+(5-4)+(6-5)...(2017-2016)+(2019-2018)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"493\" height=\"18\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661382e0cd2dc927aa2199d5b2c8e900b1fc4d77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1009=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"175\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~LarryFlora\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sum of consecutive odd numbers can be expressed as a square, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/5853ab383e03bba74a930ae738c4554da88bccd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+5+7+...+2017+2019 = 1010^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"327\" height=\"18\" />. We can modify the negative numbers in the same way by adding 1 to each negative term, factoring a negative sign, and accounting for the extra 1's by subtracting 1009. We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc17507f788a76ed5fcd66486f8170186a8df2bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1010^2-1009^2-1009$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />. Using difference of squares, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc24e4b817bd28337b808a3c0f674bd9b29d9eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1010+1009)(1010-1009)-1009 = 2019-1009 = \\boxed{1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"470\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~SigmaPiE\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of odd numbers can be represented as the number of consecutive odds starting from one, squared. Since 2019 is (2019+1)/2, there are 1010 odd numbers. Therefore, the sum of the odd numbers is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/439ea363ba8817098b3c23219af000c41c404bc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1010^2 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 1010 \\times 1010.\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The sum of even numbers up to 2018 is calculated by noting that there are 2018/2 = 1009 even numbers. Using the formula for the sum of the first n even numbers, n(n+1), we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf09a539cbbf57d14a59369399f0ae6b5774a76e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1009 \\times (1009+1) \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 1009 \\times 1010.\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The difference between these two sums is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55dbcc17e484da2b348d9a20a377a452f1928f27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1010 \\times 1010 - 1009 \\times 1010 = 1010.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b2f7f38f5e9fc197760f34adb12d9cced4d18c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1009+2019=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"217\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CRITICAL_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CRITICAL_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CRITICAL THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uMo2Jlbm7WY\">https://youtu.be/uMo2Jlbm7WY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ykNMFdRMd0o\">https://youtu.be/ykNMFdRMd0o</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p>==See Also== y\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b